# Local Development

## Prerequisites
- Docker Desktop
- Node.js 20+
{{#if FTP_ENABLED}}- `lftp` (for deployment): `brew install lftp`
{{/if}}

## Setup

```bash
git clone <repo>
cd {{PROJECT_SLUG}}
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up -d
```

Add to `/etc/hosts`:
```
127.0.0.1  {{HOSTNAME}}
```

First-time seed:
```bash
./scripts/seed-db.sh
```

Open http://{{HOSTNAME}}:{{WP_PORT}}.

## Port map

| Service | Host port | Container port |
|---|---|---|
| WordPress | {{WP_PORT}} | 80 |
| phpMyAdmin | {{PHPMYADMIN_PORT}} | 80 |
| MariaDB | {{DB_PORT}} | 3306 |

Override via `.env` (`WP_PORT`, `PHPMYADMIN_PORT`, `DB_PORT`). Defaults are
chosen to avoid collisions with other local WP projects.

{{#if SCSS_ENABLED}}## Theme dev loop

```bash
cd wp-content/themes/{{THEME_SLUG}}
npm install      # first time
npm run watch    # gulp watch + BrowserSync reload on SCSS/PHP/JS change
```

Build CSS once: `npm run build`.
{{/if}}

{{#if MULTI_LANG}}## First-time Polylang setup

After `./scripts/seed-db.sh` on a fresh install:

1. `/wp-admin/ → Languages` — add the locales you configured at scaffold time
   ({{LOCALES_CSV}}). Default is **{{DEFAULT_LOCALE}}**. Set URL mode to
   "Directory" with "Hide URL language information for the default language"
   enabled.
2. For each new page, use Polylang's "Translations" column to add per-language
   versions.
3. `/wp-admin/ → Appearance → Menus` — create a primary menu per language and
   assign each to the `primary` location.
4. Export the DB so future checkouts reproduce everything:

   ```bash
   docker compose exec database sh -lc 'mysqldump -u"$MYSQL_USER" -p"$MYSQL_PASSWORD" "$MYSQL_DATABASE" --no-create-info --skip-comments' > docs/seed/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-seed.sql
   git add docs/seed/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-seed.sql
   git commit -m "chore(seed): DB export"
   ```
{{/if}}

## Common tasks

Reset DB:
```bash
docker compose down -v && docker compose up -d && ./scripts/seed-db.sh
```

Tail WP debug log:
```bash
docker compose exec wordpress tail -f /var/www/html/wp-content/debug.log
```

Stop without losing data:
```bash
docker compose stop
```
